course: dictionary
lesson: 6848
title: One word, many meanings: outside
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word outside can change its job in a sentence. It can be a noun, an adverb, a preposition or an adjective, and its meaning changes with it. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The outside of the box was red.» Here outside is a noun, and it means the outer surface.
explain: «We played outside all afternoon.» Here outside means out in the open air, not inside a building. «Wait outside the shop for me.» Here outside tells you where: near the shop, but not in it. Ask yourself: does it show a place, a direction, or a limit?
explain: Outside can also mean beyond a limit. «Good sports clubs have strict rules against fighting outside the club» means fighting that happens away from the club, beyond its own space. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Outside has four jobs: noun, adverb, preposition and adjective.
fact: «Outside» means not inside, out in the open air.
fact: The outside of a box or house is its outer part or surface.
fact: Outside a place means near it but not in it, as in «outside the school gates».
fact: Outside can mean beyond a limit, as in «outside school hours».
exercise: «Taking breaks from screens and playing outside helps your mood.» In this sentence, what does outside mean? | Very quickly | *Out in the open air | Inside a building | Near a window
exercise: In maths, what is the outside of a shape? | Its inside corner | Its centre point | Its shadow | *Its border
exercise: What does outside mean in «Wait outside the shop for me»? | *Near the shop but not in it | Inside the shop, by the till | On the roof of the shop | Far away in another town
test: «Inside the huddle it can be more than 20 degrees warmer than outside.» What is outside in this sentence? | A hot summer day | *The cold air beyond the huddle | The warm middle of the huddle | A kind of bird
test: In science, what is «the outside of a cell»? | *Its outer surface | Its colour | Its inside centre | Its size
exam: «These pets come with one rule: never let them go outside.» What does outside mean here? | Inside the cage | Before breakfast | *Out of the house, into the open air | Under the bed
